  "body": "## What this adds\n\nA **Providers → Claude Code settings file** card that reads and patches `~/.claude/settings.json`, plus a launcher split.\n\nClaude Code's settings file takes precedence over environment variables, so a stale `env` entry silently defeats an exported `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` — and the failure presents as \"the proxy is broken\". The card makes that file a first-class, inspectable surface.\n\n**Four states**, because the interesting one is the third:\n\n| State | Rendering |\n| --- | --- |\n| not configured | neutral |\n| configured | positive |\n| **points elsewhere** | warning, **shows the current base URL and whether the token differs** before overwriting |\n| unreadable | error, and Configure refuses rather than overwriting |\n\n**The path is editable and pre-filled.** Under WSL the server's home is not the home Claude Code reads on Windows; writing the wrong file silently is the failure mode that matters most on this setup. When WSL is detected the Windows-side path is offered as a second suggestion.\n\nA sibling `settings.local.json` holding `ANTHROPIC_*` is flagged, since it overrides whatever we write.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Every other key preserved, top-level and inside `env`.\n- Backed up once to `<path>.fcc-backup`, then written via temp file + `os.replace`.\n- A file that does not parse as a JSON object is **refused, not overwritten** — and so is one whose `env` is present but is not an object, since replacing that would destroy it.\n- Values come from `local_proxy_root_url()` / `proxy_auth_token()`, never literals, so a non-default port writes a config that works.\n- The raw auth token never reaches a response body, an error detail or a status field.\n\n## Launcher split\n\n`fcc-claude` now sets **only** `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` and `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` over the inherited environment. The previous behaviour — gateway model discovery, auto-compact window, telemetry disabled, inherited `ANTHROPIC_*` cleared — is preserved verbatim as **`fcc-claude-old`**, and both are propagated through the installers, uninstallers, README, USAGE and ARCHITECTURE.\n\n## Architecture\n\n`proxy_auth` moves `cli/` → `config/`: the admin API needs it and the declared package policy does not allow `api -> cli`. `tests/contracts/test_import_boundaries.py` caught this. Callers updated, no shim left behind.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Round-tripped a copy of a real 15 KB `settings.json`** — 22 top-level keys, 99 existing `env` entries:\n\n```\ntop-level keys: 22 | has env: True | env keys: 99\nstate before: unset\nnon-env top-level keys altered: NONE\nother env entries altered: NONE\nadded env keys: ['ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN', 'ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL']\nround-trip identical to original: True\n```\n\n**Drove the real dashboard in Chrome** against a throwaway path — Configure → `Configured — pointing at this proxy`, Remove → `Not configured`, buttons disable in flight, every render comes from the server's returned status. The warning states render as intended:\n\n```\nPoints elsewhere — current base URL is http://127.0.0.1:9999, and the token\ndiffers. Configure will overwrite this.\nC:\\tmp\\claude\\uitest\\settings.local.json also sets ANTHROPIC_* variables and\ntakes precedence over the file above.\n```\n\nClicking Configure on a malformed file through the UI left it byte-identical on disk and surfaced the parse error.\n\n**HTTP layer**, all three routes:\n\n```\nAPPLY 200 -> state: configured | expected_base_url: http://127.0.0.1:8082\nUNSET 200 -> state: unset      | expected_base_url: 'http://127.0.0.1:8082'\ntoken leaked in any body: False\nreject 'relative/settings.json' -> 400 Path must be absolute\nmalformed apply -> 409 | token in detail: False | file untouched: True\nnon-loopback GET -> 403\n```\n\n**Both launchers** run Claude Code 2.1.223 and route real prompts through the proxy. The `claude.ai connectors are disabled` notice appears identically on both, so it is caused by setting `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` at all — not by the minimal environment.\n\n**Full suite: 3155 passed, 14 failed** — the documented pre-existing baseline (8 defeated by real API keys in the shell environment, 6 PowerShell installer tests), unchanged on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **Unverified:** whether dropping `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY` empties the interactive model picker. It is an interactive-only signal and could not be observed headlessly; the proxy does serve `GET /v1/models`. `fcc-claude-old` is the escape hatch if it does.\n- Unset removes only the two keys rather than restoring prior values. The `.fcc-backup` file covers recovery; a restore-on-unset would need a separate sidecar.\n- `json.dump` normalises formatting and would drop comments. Claude Code's settings file is strict JSON, and the card says so.\n- The installers now require `fcc-claude-old` to exist, so a partial install fails verification rather than silently shipping one launcher.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
