    "message": "feat(admin): configure Claude Code's settings.json from the dashboard\n\nPointing Claude Code at the proxy meant hand-editing ~/.claude/settings.json\nand getting the JSON merge right. That file also takes precedence over\nenvironment variables, so a stale entry silently defeats an exported\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and the failure looks like the proxy being broken.\n\nAdds a Providers card that reads and patches that file. It reports four\nstates — not configured, configured, points elsewhere, unreadable — and the\n\"points elsewhere\" case shows the current base URL and whether the token\ndiffers, so nothing is overwritten sight unseen. The target path is editable\nand pre-filled: under WSL the server's home is not the home Claude Code reads\non Windows, and writing the wrong file silently is the failure mode that\nmatters most here. A sibling settings.local.json holding ANTHROPIC_* is\nflagged, since it overrides whatever we write.\n\nWrites preserve every other key, back the file up once with a .fcc-backup\nsuffix, and go through a temp file plus os.replace. A file that does not parse\nas a JSON object is refused rather than overwritten, and so is one whose \"env\"\nis present but is not an object — replacing that would destroy it. Values come\nfrom local_proxy_root_url() and proxy_auth_token(), never literals, so a\nnon-default port writes a config that actually works.\n\nfcc-claude now sets only ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN over the\ninherited environment. The previous launcher — which also enables gateway model\ndiscovery, sets the auto-compact window, disables telemetry and clears\ninherited ANTHROPIC_* — is preserved verbatim as fcc-claude-old, and both are\npropagated through the installers, uninstallers, README, USAGE and ARCHITECTURE.\n\nproxy_auth moves from cli/ to config/ because the admin API needs it and the\ndeclared package policy does not allow api -> cli. Callers were updated and no\nshim was left behind.\n\nVerification:\n- Round-tripped a copy of a real 15 KB settings.json (22 top-level keys, 99\n  existing env entries): apply added exactly the two keys and altered nothing\n  else; unset restored the file to byte-equivalent original.\n- Drove the real dashboard in Chrome: Configure -> \"Configured\", Remove ->\n  \"Not configured\", buttons disable in flight, every render comes from the\n  server's returned status. Clicking Configure on a malformed file left it\n  byte-identical on disk and surfaced the parse error.\n- Both launchers run Claude Code 2.1.223 and route real prompts through the\n  proxy. The \"claude.ai connectors are disabled\" notice appears identically on\n  both, so it is caused by setting ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN at all, not by the\n  minimal environment.\n- No response body, error detail or status field carries the auth token.\n- Non-loopback callers still get 403 on all three new routes.\n- Full suite: 3155 passed, 14 failed — the documented pre-existing baseline\n  (8 defeated by real API keys in the shell environment, 6 PowerShell\n  installer tests), unchanged on unmodified main.\n\nNot done: whether dropping CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY empties\nthe interactive model picker is unverified — it is an interactive-only signal.\nfcc-claude-old is the escape hatch if it does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
